{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_06A","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is a long walk through `lib/`, folder by folder. `lib/services/` holds the business logic: every write flow opens one transaction and threads it through the repositories it calls. `lib/repositories/` is the data access: each export is one Prisma operation, and a write takes the transaction handle as a required argument, so a write outside a transaction does not compile. `lib/mappers/` turns rows into the DTOs that cross the API boundary, and `lib/dto/` names those shapes. Each domain keeps its typed errors in its own `errors.ts`, which the routes translate into status codes. `lib/agentInstances/` holds the agent profiles and the lifecycle rules, `lib/agentTerminal/` the relay and its protocol, and `lib/theme/` the palettes and styles. Next come the smaller folders, one by one, starting with the email templates and the navigation helpers."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"output_tokens":12}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"49c4fa44-2f7e-4f0a-9d3b-5a1c0e7b2d10","uuid":"u-0352"}
